**Root cause:** `src/components/Sidebar/Sidebar.browser.test.tsx:41` waits on a fixed 50ms sleep before reading the computed style, instead of polling:

```ts
it("hides the nav label and centers the icon when its container is narrow", async () => {
  const { getByText } = renderInside(140);

  const label = getByText("Posts");
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 50));          // ← fixed sleep
  expect(getComputedStyle(label).display).toBe("none");
});
```

That 50ms is a guess for how long the container-query style recalculation takes to settle. On your machine it's reliably faster than 50ms; on a shared/loaded CI or dev-machine runner it sometimes isn't, so the assertion reads the pre-update style and fails — which lines up exactly with "passes locally, fails ~1/3 of the time on the shared machine."

The test right above it (`"shows the nav label... when its container is wide"`, line 30–35) already does this the right way with `expect.poll`, which re-samples until the deadline instead of guessing a duration:

```ts
it("shows the nav label text when its container is wide", async () => {
  const { getByText } = renderInside(320);

  const label = getByText("Posts");
  await expect.poll(() => getComputedStyle(label).display).not.toBe("none");
});
```

**Fix:** replace the narrow-container test's fixed sleep with the same polling pattern:

```diff
